<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102048" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σωμά̆τ-ωσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>embodying, making of bodies</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herm.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				1.41.6
			</span></i>; <i>formation of the body,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theol.Ar.
				31
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>thickening, consolidation</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				6.11.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> Math.,
				<i>becoming solid, acquiring a third dimension,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theol.Ar.
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				36
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>the stuff of which bodies are made</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τῆς γειναμένης -ώσεως ἐποίησεν
					ἡμᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herm.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				1.41.8
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
